# patches/gates - where the build stops between its stages (issue 189)
#
# For a general audience: every patch has a priority, one number line for
# all of them. A gate is a number on that line where the build does a stage
# of its own work; nothing at or above a gate runs until everything below it
# has finished and the gate's work is done. One gate for each stage the build
# has (the owner, 2026-10-20: "However many sections we have now, that's how
# many we should have with the newly numbered system").
#
#   below 1000      source patches: applied to the server's code, and taken
#                   off again once the compile is through
#   1000            the compile and the install
#   1000 to 1999    settings and install steps, run into the installed server
#   2000            the databases brought to upstream's state
#   2000 to 8999    our own SQL (issue 189d)
#   9000            the server may start
#
# One gate a line: "number: what happens there". Read by scripts/plan-patches.
# Lines starting with "#" and blank lines are ignored.

1000: compile and install
2000: databases brought to upstream's state
9000: the server may start
